Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-22-2001||10:30 PM||||Hi fellow Fieron's, <BR>   Was anything done to the frames/chassis on t-top cars as far as stiffening ? I hope they didn't just cut the roof and not do something to the frame ?<BR>    Thanks !<P>   ††† GOD BLESS AMERICA †††||||reg||1
Z||000001||qwikgta||09-22-2001||10:49 PM||||As far as I can tell they didn't do anything to the "frame" on my car.  It was number 95 converted by C&C.  It creeks like all ttops after 13 years.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-23-2001||02:25 AM||||Hrm, my T-top car dosen't creak at all...<P>Now has 71,000miles on her, and about 1,000 of those with the low-profile 45series 17" tyres.<P>NO creaking.  Yet.  If/When it does, I'll re-do the interior and weld things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The roof section's stregenth bearing section is in the center for the T-top cars, there is quite a bit of very structual steel that is ADDED to compensate for of course cutting the side panels where the stregenth bearing steel is located for cars with (or withught, as all cars have the cutouts) sunroofs for example.<P>An X-frame as suitable for a convertible car wouldn't hurt anything though.  <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||AusFiero||09-24-2001||07:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by qwikgta:<BR><B>It was number 95 converted by C&C.  It creeks like all ttops after 13 years.<P>Rob<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well that isn't entirely true. It is the 95th 88 converted. C&C did a hell of a lot of Fieros before 88. About 1000 or so kits, many fitted by C&C were around before then. They just didn't have a factory option sticker on them is all. My deceased 86 T-topped car was one of the first. Not all t-topped cars creak either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
